  "title": "Israeli settlers escalate attacks on West Bank areas under direct Palestinian rule",
  "summary": "Israeli settlers in the occupied West Bank under direct Palestinian rule have shifted their focus to areas earmarked for a future Palestinian state, with violent attacks nearly doubling since 2025. According to a report by Yesh Din, almost two-thirds of settler violence in 2026 has occurred in these designated areas.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Israeli settlers set fire to Palestinian homes and vehicles in villages near Nablus in the northern West Bank.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "According to a report by Yesh Din, almost two-thirds of settler violence in 2026 has taken place in the so-called 'Areas A and B' - placed under Palestinian Authority governance in the 1995 Oslo accords.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The attacks have been described as part of ongoing tensions between settlers and Palestinian communities.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
